verdict.reason:
A covers every required point:
- stop paying lawyers because pre-PMF stock is worthless;
- the leaving founder goes under 5%, and 1–2% or less within the first year, even if vested;
- a no-fault, clean separation.

It also covers supporting points: about a week at minimal cost, reasonable severance, and not making lawyers judges. It notes the misconduct exception only loosely, as an assumption. B also advises stopping the lawyer fight and negotiating directly. However, it tells the founder to keep a prorated portion of vested stock for nine months of work. That contradicts the source, which says the leaving founder should give most of it back even if vested. B also gives no percentages and misses the no-fault framing.
